        "predicate": "narration_independence",
        "instruction": {
          "title": "Independence of Horizontal and Vertical Motion",
          "description": "Watch the launch: the horizontal component arrow stays constant length throughout flight, while the vertical component shrinks to zero at the peak, then grows downward during descent. The ball traces a parabolic trail. Switch to the overhead view to see the horizontal motion alone appear as a straight line. Horizontal motion is unaffected by gravity; vertical motion behaves exactly as a ball thrown straight up."
        },
